"\nTARGET 16 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_01\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 035602cc2296c24cd166885fa7772d872cd4e8fd 44d64b1b69edf5367459377a6dd47cf4c4a912e655626961549fb9d6082bb504 RANGES [[3, 19]] MASKED []\n3: ## 21:15 UTC \u2014 GENERIC_X64 (x86_64 VM) build spike\n4: \u002d Re\u002dderived a bootable **GENERIC_X64** VM/QA target onto `feature/generic\u002dx64` (off `next`),\n5:   from the stale `x64\u002dbuild\u002dfix` (~2465 commits behind). Foundation + ~18 reactive fixes;\n6:   build reached image assembly (last cores being cleared). Detached\u002dbuild workflow, logging to\n7:   `~/Development/generic\u002dx64\u002dbuild.log`. Requires the `.git` mount for docker builds from a\n8:   worktree (`scripts/image` runs `git rev\u002dparse`).\n9: \u002d **Key pivot:** dropped Intel `iris` HW GL for **llvmpipe (software GL)** \u2014 iris pulls an\n10:   unresolvable SPIR\u002dV version cascade (glslang\u002d15.1.0 vs SPIRV\u002dLLVM\u002dTranslator\u002d20.1.5 need\n11:   incompatible spirv\u002dheaders). llvmpipe is the reliable VM path anyway.\n12: \u002d Notable fixes: restore `intel\u002ducode`; graphene AVX header bug; gcc **libatomic** for x86_64;\n13:   glslang install bundled SPIRV\u002dTools libs (libplacebo link); libsamplerate `\u002dfPIC`;\n14:   dosbox/a5200/gliden64/ppsspp\u002dlr arch fixes; installer drops grub (syslinux for x86 UEFI).\n15: \u002d **Concessions (deliberate, for a fast QA boot)** tracked in fork issue **#17** (path to a\n16:   full/bare\u002dmetal build): `X64_SKIP_CORES` (parallel\u002dn64\u002dlr, flycast2021\u002dlr, duckstation\u002dlr,\n17:   idtech\u002dlr), SM8250\u002dderived emulator configs (placeholders), no HW/Vulkan accel. VM build = #16.\n18: \u002d Next: finish image (`.img.gz`), then add a VM\u002dimage output (qcow2/vdi/img) + boot\u002dtest in QEMU.\n\nTARGET 17 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_04\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 29ae001ee0227d9e3762ddf3308b06764f8dc6c4 82bebac34eb752855e8e25f98641501d4e83f49df1996c3f162bbe82d2febb92 RANGES [[3, 50]] MASKED []\n3: ## 00:20 UTC \u2014 GENERIC_X64 VM: booted all the way to EmulationStation\n4: \n5: Got the fresh `feature/generic\u002dx64` VM image to boot through to a rendering\n6: EmulationStation in QEMU (llvmpipe software GL on virtio\u002dgpu). Four x86_64\u002dspecific\n7: boot blockers, each with an aarch64 counterpart that hid the issue:\n8: \n9: 1. **UEFI shell** (earlier): mkimage didn't flag partition 1 as ESP on gpt/syslinux, so\n10:    strict UEFI wouldn't auto\u002drun `\\EFI\\BOOT\\BOOTX64.EFI`. Fixed with `set 1 esp on`.\n11: 2. **`/init` panic (error \u002d2)**: x86_64 glibc's loader is `/lib64/ld\u002dlinux\u002dx86\u002d64.so.2`,\n12:    but the base initramfs only made `/lib,/bin,/sbin`. Added an x86_64 initramfs overlay\n13:    conf (`initramfs.x86_64.conf`) creating `/lib64 \u002d> usr/lib`. aarch64's loader is\n14:    `/lib/...` so it was unaffected.\n15: 3. **Post\u002dresize \"Can't lookup blockdev\" \u2192 power\u002ddown**: first\u002dboot `fs\u002dresize` runs\n16:    `tune2fs \u002dU random`, regenerating the storage ext4 UUID. aarch64 survives because\n17:    u\u002dboot re\u002dreads the UUID at boot (`fsuuid` in `a_boot.ini`); syslinux/grub bake it\n18:    statically. Switched the x86_64 boot entries to `boot=LABEL`/`disk=LABEL` (labels\n19:    `ROCKNIX`/`STORAGE` survive resize) \u2014 matches the ROCKNIX grub generator.\n20: 4. **ES crash \"wayland not available\"** \u2014 actually sway dying first: `111\u002dsway\u002dinit`\n21:    derives the DRM card number from the first connector matching `DP|HDMI|DSI`.\n22:    virtio\u002dgpu exposes the panel as `card0\u002dVirtual\u002d1`, so `card_no` was empty \u2192\n23:    `WLR_DRM_DEVICES=/dev/dri/card` (no number) \u2192 \"Found 0 GPUs\" \u2192 no Wayland \u2192 SDL abort.\n24:    Added `Virtual` to the connector match. Real panels still match DP/HDMI/DSI first.\n25: \n26: **Why it matters:** this is the whole point of GENERIC_X64 (issue #16) \u2014 devs can now QA\n27: ES/features in a VM instead of flashing. The remaining concessions (llvmpipe vs hw GL,\n28: skipped cores) are tracked for the eventual bare\u002dmetal x64 build (issue #17).\n29: \n30: ### Debugging/QA method notes (durable)\n31: \u002d Local QA: `qemu\u002dsystem\u002dx86_64` + OVMF split firmware (writable `OVMF_VARS` copy) +\n32:   `\u002dvga virtio`. TCG (`\u002dcpu max`) works but is too slow for two boots + ES; KVM is needed\n33:   for a timely full boot.\n34: \u002d KVM access: `setfacl \u002dm u:max:rw /dev/kvm` is **reset by logind** between sessions. The\n35:   durable fix is `usermod \u002daG kvm max` + launching QEMU via `sg kvm \u002dc` (picks up the group\n36:   without re\u002dlogin).\n37: \u002d ES/other logs land on tmpfs `/var/log` (lost on shutdown). Read them **live over SSH**\n38:   (root/rocknix, hostfwd + `SSH_ASKPASS`) or **offline** with `debugfs \u002dR \"cat \u2026\"` on the\n39:   `dd`\u002dextracted ext4 partition 2. Headless UI check: QEMU monitor `screendump`.\n40: \u002d The ES crash looked like a GL/ES bug but the real cause was one layer down (sway had no\n41:   GPU). Reading `sway.log` before chasing ES saved a lot of time \u2014 verify the layer below\n42:   before blaming the app (see engineering\u002dpractices).\n43: \n44: ### Follow\u002dups\n45: \u002d Re\u002dupload the fixed, ES\u002dbooting image to the fork release.\n46: \u002d VM\u002dimage output feature (qcow2/vdi via qemu\u002dimg) \u2014 todo `x64\u002dvm\u002dimage`.\n47: \u002d Tune the placeholder emulator configs (issue #17).\n48: \u002d Consider a `run\u002dqemu` helper committed with the device docs (records the exact OVMF\n49:   invocation) so other devs can boot the image without rediscovering the flags.\n\nTARGET 18 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_05\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY e64f14757f928db78d084a1bcc9ae8ab4174e3f3 fcf44a4c99bf8f89dc1e8aa8390e8cca969df6007ec98be53059ba67e2cead7b RANGES [[3, 44]] MASKED []\n3: ## 20:55 UTC \u2014 GENERIC_X64 boots to ES in KVM, but UTM drops to UEFI shell \u2192 root cause: 4K sectors\n4: \n5: Landed the last boot blockers (sway virtio\u002dgpu connector + a self\u002dinflicted missing shebang in\n6: `start_es.sh`) and verified a **clean image auto\u002dboots to EmulationStation** in KVM. Published\n7: qcow2 + raw to the fork release.\n8: \n9: Then @maxengel reported the image still drops to the **UEFI interactive shell in UTM** on Mac\n10: (both raw and native\u002dqcow2). Spent the session pinning it down:\n11: \n12: \u002d The image is **correct**: it boots in Ubuntu OVMF, upstream EDK2 (retrage), and **qemu's own\n13:   `edk2\u002dx86_64\u002dcode.fd` (the exact firmware UTM bundles)**, across **virtio and SATA** buses.\n14: \u002d Verified the ESP is a valid EFI System partition and `BOOTX64.EFI` is a valid x86\u002d64 PE.\n15: \u002d GPT primary + backup headers intact; container format (raw vs qcow2) is irrelevant (identical\n16:   bytes; both fail in UTM).\n17: \u002d **Reproduced the failure** by forcing 4K sectors with UTM's firmware:\n18:   `\u002ddevice virtio\u002dblk\u002dpci,logical_block_size=4096,physical_block_size=4096` \u2192\n19:   `BdsDxe: failed to load Boot0001 \"UEFI Misc Device\" ... Not Found` \u2192 PXE \u2192 shell. Exactly the\n20:   user's \"`map` shows only `BLK0`/`BLK1`, no `FS0:`\".\n21: \n22: **Root cause:** OVMF/UTM firmware can't UEFI\u002dboot a disk exposed with **4096\u002dbyte logical\n23: sectors** when the GPT/FAT are laid out for 512 bytes (misreads GPT \u2192 only protective MBR \u2192 no\n24: ESP). Confirmed by UTM docs + tianocore bug 957. Fix is **VM\u002dside (present 512b sectors)**, not\n25: the image \u2014 which validated the user's instinct that the *machine config* must travel with the\n26: artifact.\n27: \n28: ### Decisions / follow\u002dups\n29: \u002d Deliver a **1\u002dclick `.utm` bundle** (config + disk in one file) with a **512b VirtIO** boot\n30:   disk baked in \u2014 the user's stated goal and the actual fix. (`x64\u002dvm\u002dimage` todo.)\n31: \u002d On \"shareable dev image\" formats: VDI is *least* universal (VirtualBox\u002donly); qcow2 covers\n32:   UTM+QEMU; VMDK is the broadest bare disk; but a bare disk still needs correct VM setup \u2014 the\n33:   real shareable unit is an **appliance** (`.utm` / OVA) that carries the config.\n34: \u002d Immediate user fix to try: switch the UTM boot drive to a 512b interface (VirtIO/SATA), not a\n35:   4K/NVMe\u002d4K disk.\n36: \u002d Captured as a Copilot memory + a new section in `generic\u002dx64\u002dvm\u002dtesting.instructions.md`\n37:   (\"Won't boot in UTM / a VM \u2192 check the disk logical sector size\").\n38: \n39: ### Method note\n40: Matching the *exact* firmware the user runs (pulled qemu's `edk2\u002dx86_64\u002dcode.fd`, the file UTM\n41: ships) + sweeping one variable at a time (firmware \u2192 bus \u2192 sector size) is what turned an\n42: un\u002dreproducible \"works for me\" into a deterministic local repro. Container format was a red\n43: herring; the disk **sector size** was the variable.\n\nTARGET 19 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_08\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 66227a8076283ff878d713d6b11c8c87a280f3af abd87edb4a3f86cbcc53750bd399eb70775451f1e28d60165d979e4a44207f77 RANGES [[3, 43]] MASKED []\n3: ## 21:30 UTC \u2014 GENERIC_X64 \"menu has no dim/blur\": root cause was disk size, not graphics\n4: \n5: **Finding.** The long\u002dhunted GENERIC_X64 ES bug (main menu opens/navigates but has no\n6: dimmed/blurred background, wrong fonts, missing help\u002dbutton glyphs) is **not** a\n7: graphics/compositor/GL bug. It is caused by an **undersized VM disk**:\n8: \n9: \u002d The raw `.img` is ~4GB (`SYSTEM_SIZE=4096` + a tiny `STORAGE` tail). `STORAGE` resizes to\n10:   fill its disk on first boot, but on a ~4GB disk it stays ~33MB and hits **100% full**.\n11: \u002d First\u002dboot `rsync /usr/config \u2192 /storage/.config` then fails with **ENOSPC**\n12:   (`rsync: write failed on .../resources/DroidSansFallbackFull.ttf: No space left on device`)\n13:   and copies **0 of 144** ES resource files.\n14: \u002d ES therefore can't resolve its `:/` resources \u2014 including `:/shaders/blur.glsl` (menu\n15:   dim/blur), `:/ubuntu_condensed.ttf`, and `:/help/*.svg`. `postProcessShader`'s shaderBatch\n16:   is null \u2192 no dim. Real hardware never hits this (storage resizes to fill the whole SD card\n17:   *before* the rsync).\n18: \n19: **Red herrings ruled out:** weston vs sway (ES makes its own Mesa GL context regardless of\n20: compositor), `glBlitFramebuffer`/`postProcessShader`, GL 3.0 core context. All downstream of\n21: the missing embedded shader.\n22: \n23: **How it was found.** SSH into the VM kept resetting and headless `screendump` was black, so I\n24: added a **serial debug console** to GENERIC_X64 (`serial\u002ddebug\u002dshell.service`: autologin root\n25: `/bin/sh` on `ttyS0`, systemd debug\u002dshell pattern since ROCKNIX strips all getty units). With a\n26: real shell, `df \u002dh /storage` (100%) + `journalctl | grep \"no space\"` made the cause obvious.\n27: Also learned: headless `screendump` needs `\u002dvnc :N` (a bare `\u002ddisplay none` captures black).\n28: \n29: **Fix (verified).** Boot on a 16GB disk \u2192 storage resizes to 11.9GB \u2192 rsync completes (144\n30: files, `blur.glsl` + fonts present, 0 ENOSPC) \u2192 main menu renders with a proper dimmed\n31: background + fonts + help icons (screenshot\u002dconfirmed).\n32: \n33: \u002d Feature branch `feature/generic\u002dx64`: committed the serial console (`a83efbd71d`); `mkimage`\n34:   now also emits a **sparse 16GB `.qcow2`** gated on a new `VM_IMAGE_SIZE` option so a 1\u002dclick\n35:   boot has adequate storage.\n36: \u002d Personal (`next`): updated `generic\u002dx64\u002dvm\u002dtesting.instructions.md` with the disk\u002dsize\n37:   section + the serial\u002dconsole technique + the `\u002dvnc` screendump note.\n38: \n39: **Follow\u002dups.** Public rocknix.org docs for GENERIC_X64 don't exist yet (target isn't upstream),\n40: so no public\u002ddocs change today. Consider whether `SYSTEM_SIZE=4096` is larger than needed for\n41: the ~1.9GB squashfs (would give more `STORAGE` headroom on small disks) \u2014 deferred, low value\n42: since the qcow2 fix covers the VM case.\n\nTARGET 20 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_10\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY f745df596b5775a7860896ca3718bc376d21c0ba bb6a107c23c1b43a5c9f21fcf21799bd99068d9a91baf48b3778348d177233b1 RANGES [[3, 31]] MASKED []\n3: ## 23:30 UTC \u2014 Reopened GENERIC_X64 artifact work around environment parity\n4: \n5: The 16 GiB qcow2 fixed storage sizing, but it did **not** satisfy the original developer\u002dQA\n6: goal: a disk image carries disk bytes only, not CPU, RAM, firmware, machine type, disk bus and\n7: sector geometry, GPU, network, audio, input, or serial configuration. Closing the VM\u002dimage\n8: task after publishing qcow2 was a scope error.\n9: \n10: **Decision:** standardize on QEMU's guest\u002dvisible machine model, not VirtualBox. VirtualBox on\n11: Apple silicon only runs Arm guests and cannot run this x86_64 image. UTM can run x86_64 via\n12: QEMU TCG on the M5 Mac; Linux uses QEMU/KVM. Host acceleration necessarily differs, but both\n13: must consume one versioned canonical profile.\n14: \n15: Baseline profile:\n16: \n17: \u002d Q35 + UEFI\n18: \u002d Haswell\u002dv4 (oldest fixed model satisfying ROCKNIX's `x86\u002d64\u002dv3` build), 4 vCPUs, 8 GiB RAM\n19: \u002d 16 GiB VirtIO disk with explicit 512\u002dbyte logical/physical sectors\n20: \u002d `virtio\u002dgpu\u002dgl\u002dpci`, `virtio\u002dnet\u002dpci`, Intel HDA, USB 3, and serial console\n21: \n22: Implemented `projects/ROCKNIX/devices/GENERIC_X64/vm/profile.json` and a single generator that\n23: runs Linux/QEMU and builds a current UTM configuration\u002dv4 `.utm.zip` from that profile. The\n24: Linux path full\u002dbooted with KVM to the serial debug shell. The UTM plist and bundle structure\n25: were validated against UTM's current Codable schema; actual launch on macOS/UTM remains the\n26: cross\u002dhost acceptance check.\n27: \n28: `tools/fork\u002dpublish\u002drelease` now generates and uploads qcow2 and `.utm.zip` from the same\n29: profile and updates existing release notes, preventing the two host environments from\n30: silently drifting.\n\nTARGET 21 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_11\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 5fd2136848fda4432cd865989b1661db57995935 236734cd5a034cb986baab795cb4c9e072abc0c41c64a48addbd29b7f28a942d RANGES [[3, 19]] MASKED []\n3: ## 16:55 UTC \u2014 UTM parity accepted; fixed upside\u002ddown cursor sprite\n4: \n5: The canonical `.utm` environment boots and otherwise works correctly on the M5 Mac, confirming\n6: the cross\u002dhost machine profile. The remaining defect was specifically the **cursor graphic**\n7: rendering upside down; movement directions and the entire UI were already correct.\n8: \n9: This isolated the defect to UTM/virtio\u002dgpu's hardware cursor plane, not input coordinates or\n10: output orientation. ROCKNIX already uses wlroots' software\u002dcursor workaround for NVIDIA, and\n11: an old QEMU quirk incorrectly applied it to unused `weston.service`; active Sway did not receive\n12: it.\n13: \n14: Fixed `111\u002dsway\u002dinit` to set `WLR_NO_HARDWARE_CURSORS=1` only for virtual DRM connectors\n15: (`Virtual\u002d*`). A rebuilt GENERIC_X64 image full\u002dbooted with Sway active, and\n16: `/var/log/sway.log` confirmed `Loading WLR_NO_HARDWARE_CURSORS option: 1`. This leaves pointer\n17: coordinates and display transforms unchanged while compositing the cursor in the correctly\n18: oriented primary plane.\n\nTARGET 22 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_23\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 9f0f8a2cdd0c4db7c9d549c17e05f9643ef18c23 d08e635ef1e99c3d0d5d3bbc86a3508056ab330aaa3f7c1a2a2fa9b6827afaa8 RANGES [[37, 44]] MASKED []\n37: ## 05:45 UTC \u2014 policy: squash upstream PRs to a single commit\n38: \n39: \u002d Dev\u002dteam preference recorded in `fork\u002dworkflow.instructions.md`: upstream PRs must\n40:   present exactly one commit for review (squash after the `\u002d\u002donto` rebase via\n41:   `git reset \u002d\u002dsoft upstream/next && git commit`). Granular history stays on\n42:   `feature/<name>`; only the disposable `pr/<name>` branch is squashed.\n43: \n\nTARGET 23 docs/work\u002dlogs/2026_07\u002dwork_logs/2026_07_24\u002dwork_log.md bounded\u002dday\u002dentry\nIDENTITY 046e2382f1bd4884aad4c96d98abb20bdec15682 d902da0c3157fd5377ff60c7336924e30063cf96ee4ffdad54414ba78f9d72fa RANGES [[126, 141]] MASKED [139]\n126: ## 17:40 UTC \u2014 feature work complete; QA integration build started\n127: \n128: \u002d L3: ThreadedCloudSync streams backend output live into the progress card.\n129: \u002d P3 MVP: cloud_content_restore (\u002d\u002dlist / \u002d\u002dall / <dirs>; copy\u002donly into\n130:   /storage/roms, CONTENTPATH root override) + ES \"RESTORE CONTENT FROM CLOUD\"\n131:   picker (GuiLoading fetch \u2192 GuiSettings dir list \u2192 background copy).\n132: \u002d Integration branches for QA (never PR): ES test/qa\u002dintegration\n133:   (cloud\u002dsync\u002dmenu + backup\u002drestore\u002ddialogs, 03a240e43), OS\n134:   test/qa\u002dintegration (cloud\u002dsaves + backuptool\u002dbaseline + ES pin), and\n135:   test/qa\u002dgeneric\u002dx64 (that + the GENERIC_X64 device) \u2014 full image building\n136:   from the cached generic\u002dx64 worktree tree.\n137: \u002d QA checklist for QEMU: Cloud Saves menu (setup QR/auto\u002dlogin, sync trio with\n138:   progress card, content restore picker), System Management (backup/restore\n139: [MASKED sensitive\u002dlabelled line; not read unredacted]\n140:   absent from zip), hooks (startup sync, game\u002dexit sync), rclone 1.74.4.\n"
